WEBVTT

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:05.760
Lately, I've been looking back.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.445
At the places I've been, the work I've done, and what I've learned.

00:00:09.445 --> 00:00:12.570
Now, as a mum of two, I wonder how I could use it all.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.815
For myself, my children, and other families.

00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:18.643
I was a curious child.

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:21.368
And that curiosity has stayed with me.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.075
I travelled, took notes, and wrote a backpacking guidebook.

00:00:26.075 --> 00:00:31.825
I also worked in tech for over eight years, organising information and sharing ideas.

00:00:32.933 --> 00:00:37.383
Now, in Britain, I share that curiosity with my two children.

00:00:38.475 --> 00:00:40.210
On days out, we find a fossil,

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.210
then look it up together at home.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.185
Music or swimming leads us to a class to try.

00:00:45.185 --> 00:00:47.235
Our discoveries become learning.

00:00:47.235 --> 00:00:50.185
And learning brings us new things to enjoy.

00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:55.303
Our family notebook filled with places, classes and discoveries.

00:00:55.303 --> 00:00:58.463
I wanted to share it, and learn from other families, too.

00:00:58.463 --> 00:01:00.613
That's how Globee began.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:03.145
Dear fellow parent.

00:01:03.145 --> 00:01:05.845
They say it takes a village to raise a child.

00:01:05.845 --> 00:01:07.920
I hope Globee can help us on that journey,

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.525
for my children, and for all our children.

00:01:10.525 --> 00:01:12.325
With love, Yewon.
